Error: apprafter::target::token_rejected

  × provider `hetzner-cloud` rejected the supplied token
  ╰─▶ apprafter::provider::hetzner_api_error
      
        × hetzner-cloud GET <HCLOUD>/v1/locations failed (status
        │ 401): unauthorized: unable to authenticate
        help: The Hetzner Cloud API returned a non-2xx response. Common
              causes:
              • 401 unauthorized — the stored API token was rotated or
              revoked. Run `apprafter target add <name> --renew --token <new>`
              to refresh it.
              • 403 forbidden — the token's project lacks permission for this
              resource type.
              • 429 rate limit — back off and retry; if persistent, the
              project may need a quota increase.
              • 5xx — provider-side outage; check https://status.hetzner.com/.
              Re-run `apprafter doctor` to confirm reachability after fixing
              the root cause.
      
  help: The provider's read-only credential check returned 401 / unauthorized.
        Either the token was mistyped, never had the right scopes, or has been
        rotated / revoked since you copied it.
        • Verify the token at https://console.hetzner.cloud/projects →
        Security → API Tokens. It must say `Read & Write` next to the project.
        • Copy the token again (it's 64 ASCII chars, no prefix) — common
        cause: trailing newline from a clipboard manager.
        • If you're rotating, run `apprafter target add <name> --renew --token
        <new>` instead of re-creating the target.
        • Pass `--no-ping` to skip the check if you're seeding a target
        offline (CI sandbox, intermittent network).

